From: enij90 <226572015+enij90@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: HDR output metadata and BT.2020 colorimetry

The DP connector had neither HDR_OUTPUT_METADATA nor Colorspace, so a
compositor could not switch an external monitor to HDR: gamescope offers
the toggle, but the sink never gets the HDR InfoFrame and stays in SDR.

Attach both properties to the external DP connector (not eDP). With
metadata set, pack it as an HDR Metadata InfoFrame SDP (CTA-861 DRM
InfoFrame without checksum, DP 1.4a) and send it on generic SDP slot 2.
Slot 0 carries the VSC SDP, now also used for RGB with BT.2020
colorimetry when the sink supports VSC. Both are programmed with the
stream, so a change of either takes a modeset (atomic_check); metadata
the sink's EDID does not accept is rejected there.

A reduced port to 7.2 of the DP part of Xilin Wu's "drm/msm/dp: Add static
HDR support for DP and eDP" v2 (freedreno, October 2026): same packing,
same Generic2 registers, without its eDP, PSR, video-test, max bpc and
link-state rework. Output depth stays the EDID/bandwidth choice.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
@@ -2560,6 +2560,7 @@
 	phy = ctrl->phy;
 
 	msm_dp_panel_disable_vsc_sdp(ctrl->panel);
+	msm_dp_panel_disable_hdr_sdp(ctrl->panel);
 
 	/* set dongle to D3 (power off) mode */
 	msm_dp_link_psm_config(ctrl->link, &ctrl->panel->link_info, true);
@@ -2590,6 +2591,7 @@
 	phy = ctrl->phy;
 
 	msm_dp_panel_disable_vsc_sdp(ctrl->panel);
+	msm_dp_panel_disable_hdr_sdp(ctrl->panel);
 
 	msm_dp_ctrl_mainlink_disable(ctrl);
 
